{"chunk_id": "3aac40225d8c", "text": "Hotravahana explains to a sage that the distressed maiden before them is Amva, eldest daughter of the king of Kasi and his own granddaughter. During the swayamvara of Amva and her sisters Amvika and Amvalika, Bhishma stormed the assembly, defeated the gathered kings, and carried the princesses away to marry his half\u2011brother Vichitravirya. Amva revealed that she had already chosen King Salwa in her heart, and Bhishma, acknowledging this, allowed her to go. Yet Salwa rejected her, doubting her purity after the abduction. Ashamed to return home and consumed by grief, Amva seeks guidance. The sage Akritavrana suggests either persuading Salwa to accept her or having Parashurama defeat Bhishma. Gradually Amva\u2019s anguish turns toward vengeance against Bhishma. When Parashurama arrives, she falls before him and begs rescue from her suffering.\nAmba recounts Bhishma\u2019s abduction, Salwa\u2019s rejection, and appeals to Parashurama for justice or vengeance against Bhishma.\nThemes: rejected love, honor and shame, revenge quest, kshatriya duty, appeal to divine justice", "vector": [-0.010592382401227951, -0.02540302835404873, 0.003787761088460684, 0.009864864870905876, -0.0303821824491024, 0.02984822541475296, -0.015685001388192177, -0.019729729741811752, -0.011046245694160461, -0.029901620000600815, 0.0030936163384467363, -0.004271660000085831, 0.017714040353894234, -0.003477398306131363, -0.015124346129596233, 0.0003278832882642746, 0.048189666122198105, -4.1480780055280775e-05, 0.00764894112944603, -0.02902059070765972, 0.009577862918376923, -0.00015059270663186908, 0.0042182644829154015, 0.02692480757832527, -0.042636506259441376, 0.02504260651767254, 0.017073290422558784, -0.022279376164078712, 0.001765397028066218, -0.02066415548324585, -0.019716380164027214, -0.004518615547567606, -0.008222945965826511, -0.016699520871043205, -0.033799510449171066, -0.002706497209146619, -0.001334893750026822, -0.01015186682343483, 0.018